    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "The idea of a \"slop file\" is interesting, but I'm worried about the actual staff workload. When the intake is at its most chaotic, everything feels a bit like it's just being thrown into a pile and left to scramble. Is there a way to structure the workflow so that the \"chaos\" doesn't result in materials just vanishing into the shuffle?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
