      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Implementing a standardized workflow where every item is immediately placed into numbered, labeled temporary containers based on broad subject headings can prevent loss even before full classification is complete. This approach ensures that no material enters a true \"pile\" by tying each piece to a traceable bin, significantly reducing the risk of items vanishing into the shuffle during chaotic intake periods. Experts often recommend pairing anyone's labor-intensive sorting with a simple digital log to track bin locations and provenance without the full burden of assigning complex call numbers.",
